msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:14
#: 55ed43a9c3bc4964bb14992453794831
msgid "Gazebo is a well-known and respected robotics simulator, and is also the official DARPA Virtual Robotics Simulator. No current release has built-in support for ArduPilot,  however. (Previous PRs for built-in support were not merged as of April-2017)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:19
#: a89cda17ebd24f1e85d89fc0eda11ac6
msgid "If you find that some of these instructions are outdated, please open an issue for the ardupilot_wiki repository on github."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:23
#: a802fff87c884e23b650b9a8bb9a2eef
msgid "Gazebo is particularly useful for defining autonomous indoor flights or swarms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:28
#: 7faf67dd3f8d41bd92c99d82ce24ebe3
msgid "Preconditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:30
#: 7b574e49666647fe948b6583450e3b2c
msgid "We recommend Ubuntu starting from 16.04 or 18.04 as those were  the platform used for testing this approach. They are also known to be compatible with SITL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:32
#: b833789992614cc6bab5afbd03e60b9d
msgid "We will be using a standard version of ArduPilot but a custom plugin for Gazebo, until the gazebo plugin gets merged into Gazebo-master."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:34
#: 4555d0b3671f4626b1007beda70ec103
msgid "This plugin can be used with or without ROS integration. In both case we recommend to use Gazebo from the OSRF repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:42
#: 004f4196ad834d6ba2d76fcace0cd439
msgid "The plugin we will be using works with gazebo versions 7 to 9. We recommend gazebo9 as the new development will append on this version. It isn't available for older versions of  Ubuntu though, so you may need to use an earlier version depending on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:50
#: 04730ee8b0084b938d2b0c35cd5f61b0
msgid "The first time gazebo is executed requires the download of some models and it could take some time, so please be patient. Let's give a try."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:56
#: 7f1227c511a44eae8d0b411a81c395ff
msgid "It should open an empty world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:59
#: 6d18e1c58a1349d2bd17af5f1d4d4a5e
msgid "Plugin installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:61
#: 4c2c18be0edc4b30b3ebd0e794231561
msgid "The following plugin is a pure Gazebo plugin, so ROS is not needed to use it. You can still use ROS with Gazebo with normal gazebo-ros packages. We have  two version of the plugin : khancyr and SwiftGust one's. The one from `khancyr <https://github.com/khancyr/ardupilot_gazebo>`__ is the original one. It is stable and only has necessary file to work. The one from `SwiftGust <https://github.com/SwiftGust/ardupilot_gazebo>`__  has more examples and a little bit more documentation. Both use the same plugin, they only differ in the documentation and examples they provide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:67
#: 2e610237ae7c4f1ba279247426d6bdf6
msgid "We will be using khancyr plugin for the following explanation. First clone it somewhere in your home directory. (If you need help with git, please see :ref:`installed git <git-install>`, :ref:`forked <git-fork>` and :ref:`cloned <git-clone>`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-gazebo-legacy.rst:80
#: 91b8c2a8e0024d6e80f519056513b65b
msgid "These instructions will clone the repository  into the ardupilot_gazebo directory, and create a new build directory within it. The plugin will then be  compiled and installed  in the Gazebo plugin directory."
msgstr ""

